Subject: [PATCH] hw/arm/xen_arm: register ioreq server before initializing RAM
Upstream-Status: Pending

xen_arm_init() creates the guest RAM regions (xen_init_ram()) before
calling xen_register_ioreq(). The mapcache is only initialized inside
xen_register_ioreq() (xen_do_ioreq_register() -> xen_map_cache_init()).

vhost-net backends are created from -netdev in qemu_create_late_backends(),
i.e. before the machine is initialized, and register a memory listener on
address_space_memory at that point. When xen_init_ram() then adds the
xen.ram.lo/hi regions, vhost_region_add_section() resolves the host
pointer of each section with memory_region_get_ram_ptr() ->
qemu_map_ram_ptr() -> xen_map_cache(), which dereferences the still NULL
mapcache and QEMU crashes with SIGSEGV right after the vhost devices are
initialized.

The xen-troops QEMU 7.0 based tree called xen_register_ioreq() before
xen_init_ram(), so this did not happen there. Restore that order.

--- a/hw/arm/xen_arm.c
+++ b/hw/arm/xen_arm.c
@@ -235,10 +235,17 @@
         return;
     }
 
-    xen_init_ram(machine);
-
+    /*
+     * Register the IOREQ server (which also initializes the mapcache) before
+     * creating the RAM regions. Memory listeners registered earlier, e.g. by
+     * vhost-net backends created from -netdev, resolve the host pointer of
+     * each RAM section in region_add via xen_map_cache(), which dereferences
+     * the not-yet-initialized mapcache and crashes QEMU otherwise.
+     */
     xen_register_ioreq(xam->state, machine->smp.cpus, &xen_memory_listener);
 
+    xen_init_ram(machine);
+
     create_pcie(xam);
 
 #ifdef CONFIG_TPM
